# Internal strategy docs — LOCAL ONLY, never published.
# This repository is the consumer-facing front for developers and companies
# using varve. The founder thesis contains competitive teardowns, pricing, the
# open-core boundary, and candid risk assessments. None of it belongs in a
# public repo. Keep product docs for users in a separate directory (see below).
docs/

# Local drafts — session logs captured automatically, before a human publishes.
# Never committed: this is the privacy boundary (thesis §6.3).
_drafts/
**/_drafts/

# Personal Claude Code settings — permission modes are a local trust decision
# for this machine, not something to hand every contributor who clones the repo.
# Both files are ignored: settings.json was carrying defaultMode
# "bypassPermissions", which is exactly the thing this rule exists to keep out
# of a public repo. If genuinely shared, reviewable settings are ever needed,
# add a narrowly-scoped file and un-ignore that one deliberately.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Node (for when the CLI exists)
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Lavish review artifacts — local scratch surfaces for design review, not product.
.lavish/
